            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.5.1 Excretion in Human Beings"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.664,
            0.9,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The excretory system of human beings (Fig. 5.13) includes a pair of kidneys, a pair of ureters, a urinary bladder and a urethra. Kidneys are located in the abdomen, one on either side of the backbone. Urine produced in the kidneys passes through the ureters into the urinary bladder where it is stored until it is released through the urethra.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.781,
            0.9,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How is urine produced? The purpose of making urine is to filter out waste products from the blood.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Just as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { C O _ { 2 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "is removed from the blood in the lungs, nitrogenous waste such as urea or uric acid are removed from blood in the kidneys. It is then no surprise that the basic filtration unit in the kidneys,",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
